{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the people were as complainers</b> — Ibn Ezra said (on Numbers 11:1) that it is from the root און, wickedness, as in \"the devices of your און\" (Jeremiah 4:14) — that they spoke words of wickedness. But this is not correct, for why would Scripture conceal their sin and not state it, as it did in all other places? And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that when they journeyed far from Mount Sinai, which had been near settled habitation, and entered into the great and terrible wilderness on the first journey, they were distressed in themselves, saying: \"What shall we do and how shall we live in this wilderness, and what shall we eat and what shall we drink, and how shall we endure the toil and affliction, and when shall we emerge from it?\" — from the language of \"Why should a living man יתאונן, a man, complain about his sins\" (Lamentations 3:39), which is an expression of suffering and distress over oneself. And likewise \"בן אוני\" (Genesis 35:18) — son of my suffering, and \"the fishermen will אנו and mourn\" (Isaiah 19:8). And since Scripture said that they were suffering and distressed, it has already alluded to and recounted the sin, for it said <b>as complainers</b> — for they were speaking out of the bitterness of their soul, as suffering people do. And it was evil in the eyes of YHWH, for they should have gone after Him with joy and gladness of heart on account of all the goodness He had given them, yet they behaved as though coerced and constrained, complaining and rebelling against their situation. And therefore it says in the second instance: \"And the children of Israel returned and wept again\" (Numbers 11:4), for their first sin was to complain about the lack of enjoyments in the wilderness, and they returned again to do the same thing, and did not take rebuke from the fire of HaShem that had burned among them."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "n/a"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:28.578093629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}